              "value": "={{ \n  JSON.stringify([{\n    \"role\": \"user\",\n    \"content\": `Create a presentation in Marp Markdown format based on the following input.\n\nSTRICT LAYOUT RULES:\n1. Frontmatter: The very first lines of your response MUST be the YAML frontmatter provided below. Do not include any text, greetings, or \"Sure, here is your presentation\" before it.\n2. Content Splitting: You MUST create a NEW SLIDE (using '---') for every distinct section or major topic.\n3. \"One Header\" Rule: Never put two \"## H2 Headers\" on the same slide. If you start a new ## Header, you MUST put '---' before it.\n4. Bullet Limits: Maximum 5 bullet points per slide. If there are more, split them into two slides (e.g., \"Key Areas Part 1\" and \"Key Areas Part 2\").\n5. Strict Mathematical Formatting: You MUST format ALL mathematical formulas, variables, and equations using strict LaTeX syntax. \n   - For inline equations, enclose the math in single dollar signs with NO spaces between the dollar sign and the math (e.g., $E=mc^2$). \n   - For standalone block equations, use double dollar signs with NO spaces between the dollar signs and the math (e.g., $$\\\\frac{dT}{dt} = -k(T - T_{ambient})$$). \n   - Never leave equations as plain text. Ensure all variables (like 'x', 'y', 'T') are consistently formatted in LaTeX.\n6. Raw Output: Output raw Markdown text only. Do not wrap the response in markdown code blocks (\\`\\`\\`). Ensure the very first line of the output is the opening '---' of the frontmatter.\n\n---\nmarp: true\ntheme: default\nmath: mathjax\npaginate: true\nsize: 16:9\nstyle: |\n  section {\n    font-size: 25px;\n    padding: 40px;\n    justify-content: center; /* Keeps content centered vertically */\n  }\n  h1 {\n    font-size: 40px;\n    color: #0288d1;\n  }\n  h2 {\n    font-size: 35px;\n    color: #333;\n  }\n---\n\nInput Data: ${$('SlideContentGenerator').item.json.data}`\n  }])\n}}"
